there's a lot of misinformation about  the upcoming  election we want to clear that up for  our viewers  and i have clark county registrar joe  gloria here to help clear this  up we are in front of the room where the  ballots will be  counted and that's one question how can  voters be sure  that their ballot was received and will  be counted  all voters will have the opportunity to  go on our website  through registered voter services they  can  log in and there's information there  that tells them what the status of their  ballot is  or they can always call 702 455 vote  and speak with one of our customer  service representatives who can answer  those questions for them  there is this push to vote in person  in the middle of the pandemic what would  you say to that  we've made it available in the primary  we had limited resources and  availability  that won't be the case for the general  we have a full early voting schedule 35  sites scheduled over 14 days  and also on election day there will be  125 vote centers  available and also important to note all  early voting and all election day vote  centers  will also serve as mail ballot drop-off  locations  there is a concern about voter fraud if  there are  extra ballots by mailboxes especially  apartment complexes  or someone picks up a ballot that's not  theirs that they can fill it out  sign it what can you say about voter  fraud  well first off that would be an illegal  action it would be against the law for  anybody to vote a ballot that is not  theirs  however we have several checks in place  number one being every ballot that comes  in has to be signed  we verify that signature to make sure it  matches what's in the database  to verify their identity and there are  several steps that we have as far as  security also  leading into the tabulation of that  ballot president donald trump  has suggested voting twice what would  you say to that  that would be an illegal action  and it's unfortunate that those types of  statements are made i would discourage  any voter from trying to do so we will  definitely know  if you've casted two ballots and we will  go after  any voter who is illegally voting twice  southern nevada las vegas it's a  transient  location and especially now with the  pandemic and job losses  people might be in between homes  how can you be sure that they will  receive a ballot  voters need to make sure that they're  checking to be sure that their  information is correct  so now is the time to update your  information if you've moved  because mail ballots are not forwardable  whatever address we send it to if  there's nobody there  it gets returned to us so voters please  go  online if you have a nevada driver's  license or id and update your  information  or before the october 6 deadline get a  form filled out with the updated  information and get it to our office so  we can get your ballot to you  the usps sent a postcard then the  secretary of state  sent another postcard they both said two  different things can you clear this up  we want to make sure that voters are  aware in clark county and really the  state of nevada  you do not need to apply for a mail-in  ballot  all active registered voters will be  sent according to statute av4 a mail  ballot  so you do not need to submit a request  so it was a little confusing in the usps  mailer  but we want to make that clear you will  receive your ballot if you're actively  registered  the primary you mentioned there were  limited resources there were long  lines what is your prediction for  election night and can you talk about  the locations and again the difference  well we'll still have the same safety  procedures in place  we're trying to provide a safe  environment there's plenty of  disinfecting equipment master being  provided  face shields are being provided there's  a separator a plexiglas shield where  people sign in to vote and we're  creating  what we call a voting cubicle in all of  our stations to keep people safe while  they vote  we'll encourage people to social  distance and we'll encourage them to  wear a mask and we'll have masks  available for those who forget to bring  one  and can you run down some numbers how  many locations how many voting machines  how many workers and volunteers the  number of machines varies by side  according to how much room we have but  for the early voting process  over 14 days we'll have 35 teams  scheduled to go out  and set up on a daily basis also for  election day there will be 125  vote centers available for voters and  again i emphasize  both early voting and election day sites  will also serve as male ballot drop-off  locations  for anybody who wants to drop off their  ballot instead of putting it in the post  office  do you need additional election workers  and is it a challenge  finding them because of the pandemic and  many of them are seniors  we were short workers in the month of  august but once i put the call out  we got help from the county commission  we got help from several third party  groups that work with us regularly and  we're looking good to supply workers for  125 sites on election day and the early  voting program  however we're still looking for people  who have the ability to translate  in spanish and filipino so if you're  able to work and interested please  contact our office  misinformation have you ever seen it  like this  leading up to an election every election  is a challenge this is my  presidential election so i've seen quite  a bit of misinformation  that goes out it's our job to make sure  we get the good information out in doing  interviews like this that's what exactly  what we try to do  voters keep an eye on the mail you'll be  getting a sample ballot filled with  accurate information  a mail ballot supplement and your mail  ballot impacted we're also doing a  virtual town hall tomorrow night  that people can log into and watch  please watch that we'll be providing  a lot of good information in that town  hall if i'm a voter in nevada what are  three things i need to know voters in  nevada need to know  that you need to update your information  we want to send a mail ballot to the  correct address to make sure that you  get it  voters in nevada also need to know that  we have in-person voting  ability for early voting and election  day  and finally i would express to all  voters the integrity of the process in  elections is something that we take very  seriously  not just in clark county but at the  state level with the secretary of  state's office  we will do everything on our power to  make sure that we process ballots  correctly  and everything is done to uphold the  integrity of the process  do you think clark county  will have results on election night  there will be no final results on  election night  we will definitely be reporting an  unofficial total  for our in-person early voting and  election day sites minus the provisional  votes  but the mail ballots will be counted for  several days after election day so our  final unofficial won't be available to  well  after election day for anyone who  who may not know what is your role and  how is it different  from the secretary of state well the  secretary of state  oversees the entire state i'm only  responsible for clark county  although the majority of voters in the  state of nevada reside in clark county  so i'm responsible for the local  activities with all elections  the secretary of state monitors the  entire state  estimate total voters in clark county  1.2 million at this point  how has the pandemic increased the cost  of this election as opposed to previous  elections  oh there has been a significant increase  in cost um  we're providing mail ballots to every  active voter that's not something we  normally do  in a big election comparing it to the  2018 2016  we would send out maybe 70 or 80 000  mail ballots  compared to the 1.2 million that we'll  be sending out  the processing of those mail ballots  also we had to incur several  costs and the pandemic has caused us to  make sure  that we have plenty of safety equipment  disinfectant mass  all that's necessary to keep our workers  and our voters safe as they're casting  their ballot  any concerns about election security  and in particular cyber security  cyber security is an issue that's never  going away it's a constant battle  we've taken extreme steps here in clark  county  and complements to our central i.t  department that stays on top of that for  us  we've done everything we can here  locally to make sure that all of our  information is safe  important to keep in mind our tabulation  system is completely isolated there's no  connection to the internet and every one  of our in-person  uh voting systems is also isolated so  there's no access to the internet  so we've done considerable work there  and we feel comfortable that we've done  everything we can  so there have been no hacks or anything  this year  not that i'm aware of do you know how  many attempts there might have been  no no anything you want to add  we want voters to cast their ballot  we've done a lot of work to make sure  that we're prepared  to support in a very challenging time  with a pandemic  voters keep in mind that if you're  concerned at all make use of the mail  and ballot keeping in mind also  this is the longest ballot we've ever  seen in clark county vote it in the  comfort of your home do your research  mark your ballot and send it back make  sure you've signed the return  envelope not the ballot the return  envelope  send it to us or drop it off and we'll  make sure that that ballot gets  processed and counted  thank you so much less than 50 days from  the election  if you have questions let us know we  will try to get them answered for you  in north las vegas vanessa murphy 8 news  now
 

